From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: The desktop's frame for windows with a caption (xdg-decoration).

Under Wayland, Wine drew windows with a caption (UnrealGameSync, installers, Wine's own tools)
with a frame and title bar of Windows inside the surface, where winex11 leaves them to the
window manager.

With a compositor that offers zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 (KWin, GNOME, wlroots), every toplevel
gets a decoration object, and its mode follows the window: server-side for a managed window with
a caption whose visible rect is not its whole window rect, client-side otherwise. That is what
winex11 decides: windows that took the frame area for their client, even only the caption's
(Unreal's, which draw their own title bar; Tauri's maximized ones, the new Epic Games Launcher),
or with Decorated off, get no frame from the desktop. GetWindowStyleMasks tells win32u that the desktop
draws the caption and the border: they leave the visible rect, the surface, and are not drawn.
The size the compositor configures is then the surface's, the visible rect, and the window rect
gets what the frame stands for around it; a configure without a size keeps the window's own.
xdg-decoration-unstable-v1.xml is the one of wayland-protocols (MIT).

